{#
    The button that starts an attempt, as a hookable of its own so that the option to keep the card
    sits above it rather than below. Disabled here and enabled by the script once the gateway's
    frames report ready: a page whose script never ran shows a button that does nothing rather
    than one that promises to.

    Marked as belonging to the new-card path, like the fields, so that choosing a saved card puts
    it away — that path has a button of its own. `label` is optional: the account's add-a-card
    page includes this file with a label of its own.
#}
{#
    On a method that takes payment later the button does not pay: it saves the card for this
    order, and saying "Pay" there would tell the shopper the opposite of what happens. Read off
    the pay page's context when there is one; the account page includes this file directly, with
    no hook around it and a label of its own.
#}
{% set card_on_file = hookable_metadata is defined ? hookable_metadata.context.nmi.card_on_file|default(false) : false %}
{% set default_label = card_on_file ? 'jpm_martin_sylius_nmi.shop.pay.put_card_on_file'|trans : 'jpm_martin_sylius_nmi.shop.pay.pay_now'|trans %}
<button
    type="button"
    data-nmi-pay-button
    class="btn btn-primary"
    data-nmi-new-card-only
    disabled
    {{ sylius_test_html_attribute('nmi-card-pay') }}
>
    {{ label|default(default_label) }}
</button>
